  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: a3d2b5e5b8bd75781820de5be38f0970, type: 3}
  m_Name: ExhibitData_radio
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::ExhibitData
  exhibitName: THE RADIO
  pages:
  - "Before the internet, before TV, the radio was\nthe most exciting invention in
    the world!\nFamilies would gather around it every evening\nto listen to music,
    news, and stories together\njust like you might watch a show as a family today.\n
    \nIn 1901, Guglielmo Marconi sent the first ever\nradio signal across the entire
    Atlantic Ocean.\nPeople thought he was making it up how could\nsound travel invisibly
    through the air?!"
  - "In 1938 a radio drama called \"War of the Worlds\"\npretended that aliens were
    invading Earth.\nThousands of people who tuned in late\nthought it was a real
    news report and panicked!\n \nRadio waves are passing through your body\nright
    now as you read this. You just can't feel them.\nThey carry signals for phones,
    Wi-Fi, and yes\nstill radio stations broadcasting music every day. \U0001F4FB"
  exhibitIllustration: {fileID: 1875917246518206917, guid: 7b428f84e9c0a67dca605b8f1b8e9ad8, type: 3}
  narratorClip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 9a08f3c688aa6a0d0b4b4b8abef99169, type: 3}
